[~accountid:5ecfd175a04d9c0c220cbb06] Has this agreement been signed already, and where does the template come from? This one seems to be outdated, and doesn’t follow the DSA template we are currently using, in particular, for Bolt Rewards partnerships. While I wasn’t involved in the DSA negotiation process, and it might be too late to change it, I urge you to loop the privacy team in in earlier stages, and we’ll be able to provide you with the correct template.



Regarding the governing law - so, they want the main agreement to be governed by Estonian laws, and the DSA - to be governed by Malta laws? I see no practical reason for this.



What I am referring to is {{12.8. Any matter, claim or dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, whether}}
{{contractual or non-contractual, shall be governed by and determined in accordance with the laws}}
{{of Estonia.}}



As they haven’t disputed the clause 12.8, I suggest providing them with the following explanation:

{quote}Clause 12.8 of the agreement states that any dispute - whether contractual or non-contractual - will be governed by Estonian law. Since this clause hasn’t been disputed, it means there’s already agreement on Estonia as the legal jurisdiction for the main contract.

Switching to Malta law for the DSA while keeping Estonian law for the main agreement would create unnecessary confusion and inconsistency. Using one governing law throughout ensures clarity and avoids potential conflicts in interpretation.

For these reasons, we believe it’s best to keep Estonian law for both the main agreement and the DSA to maintain consistency and avoid complications.{quote}

