Hi [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] / [~accountid:63ee3904601ad5efa51309ee] a few comments on the agreement: 

# What is the total value of this agreement (I appreciate it will be 8x 498 plus VAT) for the pods themselves - but what are also the installation and collection costs? It would be good to understand the total transaction value so I can tailor my approach to amending this agreement, accordingly (also relevant for my point below regarding limitation of liability). 
# The agreement refers to {color:#0747a6}Pod Rent's General Terms & conditions of Supply - please can we be provided with these asap {color}as they form part of the agreement. {color:#ff5630}Provided {color}
# {color:#0747a6}We’d need to insert a general clause that the Supplier warrants to provide the services in accordance with Good Industry Practice (the exercise of that degree of skill, diligence, prudence and foresight which would reasonably and ordinarily be expected from a skilled and experienced person engaged in providing services which are the same as, or similar to, the services being provided in this Rental Agreement) and that the Supplier will at all times comply with all Applicable Laws (any applicable law, statute, bye law, regulation, order, regulatory policy, compulsory guidance or industry code of practice, rule of court or directive, judgment, or delegated or subordinate legislation in force from time to time). {color}-Perhaps this is covered in their T&C’s - but for the time being there is nothing of this sentiment at all in the contract.- 
# Please note clause 8 for on the day of installation: “When receiving the workspaces included therein, the Customer _shall inspect, without undue delay, that the workspaces are as described and to note any functional issues or flaws. These should be reported immediately, if possible, to the supplier's installation team and to the supplier in writing via email.”_
# I am not happy with clause 10 - them limiting their liability - it is far too broad. If we know what the total transaction value is - we can perhaps commercially agree to limit their liability to this value? If so, I propose as follows: {color:#0747a6}We can concede on ‘indirect or consequential losses’. But we will not agree to limit the Supplier’s liability with regard to direct damages caused. Happy to provide alternative drafting for clause 10 such as: {color}

{color:#0747a6}10.1 Subject to Clauses 10.2 and 10.3, the Supplier's aggregate liability to the Customer, whether in contract, tort, misrepresentation or in respect of restitution, under or in connection with this Rental Agreement shall be limited to 40,000 GBP [transaction value]. {color}
{color:#0747a6}10.2 Subject to Clause 10.3, neither party shall be liable to the other party, whether in contract, tort, breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, for any indirect, consequential or special loss arising out of, or in connection with, this Rental Agreement.{color}
{color:#0747a6}10.3 Notwithstanding Clause 10.2, the Supplier acknowledges and agrees that the following types of losses are deemed to be a non-exhaustive list of losses which are capable of recovery by the Customer under this Rental Agreement:{color}
{color:#0747a6}a) additional and/or administrative costs and expenses incurred by the Customer;{color}
{color:#0747a6}b) any fines, penalties, sanctions and costs and expenses incurred by the Customer arising out of or in connection with any failure by the Supplier to comply with any Applicable Laws or any act or omission of the Supplier which causes the Customer to fail to comply with any Applicable Law.{color}
# {color:#ff5630}-Clause 12 - periodic inspections are fine provided we have prior written notice of at least 3 working days and that they will be carried out so as to cause minimal disruptions to our business operations.- {color}{color:#ff5630} No need to include this as dealt with under the T&Cs. {color}
# Clause 13 - do we have such contents insurance already? Do we know the replacement value of the goods? [~accountid:62a3287576c0360069f59b72] for visibility too. 

I trust the above is clear - but please let me know if not. I have set out in {color:#0747a6}blue colour {color}text that can hopefully be easily lifted and sent to the supplier/PodRent by email. The text in black is internal - please do not include that in your email to the supplier. 

Best, 

Liisa

